<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antigonus III Doson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 263–<a href="/years/221-bce">221 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a> III Doson was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> from 229 BCE. Called in by the Achaean League against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleomenes-iii">Cleomenes III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, he took cities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a>, including Orchomenus and Mantinea in 223 BCE, and defeated Cleomenes at Sellasia in 222 BCE. He organised a Hellenic League under Macedonian leadership.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antigonus-iii-doson.jpg" alt="Antigonus III Doson" width="320" height="150" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: uploader - Bjankuloski06 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antigonus_Doson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
